  "direction": "Tactic-prediction on a synthetic arithmetic / propositional logic prover. Implement a tiny sequent-calculus prover for propositional logic in Python (rules as tactics) and generate 20k random provable sequents with proofs. Train a small transformer or MLP policy to pick the next rule; compare best-first search guided by the policy against breadth-first and a hand-written heuristic on proofs found within 100 expansions, for formulas larger than those in training. Keep it a small CPU study with reimplemented baselines, at least 5 seeds where cheap, and report negative or mixed results plainly.",
